{
    "background_story": "Ares was a lone wolf who roamed the vast, snow-covered territories of the north. Unlike his packmates, he never felt the urge to mate or settle down. Instead, he reveled in his freedom, traveling far and wide, and answering to no one. Ares' independence was both a blessing and a curse. He had no one to share his joys or sorrows with, but he also had no one to hold him back. His unmated status allowed him to focus on his own survival, honing his skills as a hunter and a warrior. Despite his solitary nature, Ares was not antisocial; he would occasionally join other wolves for short periods, sharing his knowledge and experience before moving on. His legend grew among the wolf community, and many whispered about the mysterious, unmated Ares, who lived life on his own terms.",
